P4C.1 spike complete — report-only, docs-only.

**Decisions recorded** (feeds PLAN.md D05), appended to `docs/plan/phases/phase-04-report.md`:
- **D5.1 local-event path** — reuse standard `calendarEvent`, no parallel backend; requires core additive work (origin marker + visibility-service change + provider-optional composer).
- **D5.2 app boundary** — local-event path and calendar surface stay core; an app owns only opt-in extras.
- **D5.3 sharing rights** — reuse channel `visibility` + per-user ownership; creator = owner for local events.
- **D5.4 capability matrix** — create pushable, update/delete read-back-only, recurrence import-metadata-only, attendee create provider-dependent.
- 10 concrete gaps recorded before any metadata/service extension.

**Key finding:** association-less events are spliced out by the per-user visibility query hook (`apply-calendar-events-visibility-restrictions.service.ts:134`), and apps cannot register query hooks/drivers — so local events cannot be app-owned.

