ndar/services/microsoft-calendar-create-event.service.ts` | `microsoftClient.api('/me/calendar/events').header('Prefer','outlook.timezone=\"UTC\"').post(...)` (lines 36–39) |\n| CalDAV | `.../calendar-event-creation-manager/drivers/caldav/services/caldav-create-event.service.ts` | `client.createCalendarObject({ calendar, filename, iCalString })` (line 63), using `ical-generator` |\n\nPayload mappers:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-creation-manager/drivers/utils/to-google-event-input.util.ts` (adds `hangoutsMeet` conference when requested)\n- `.../drivers/utils/to-microsoft-event-input.util.ts` (converts instant → wall-clock in event time zone; `teamsForBusiness` online meeting)\n- Module: `.../calendar-event-creation-manager.module.ts` (providers: composer, CreateCalendarEventService, three create drivers; imports `CalendarEventImportManagerModule`, `CalDavDriverModule`, `OAuth2ClientManagerModule`)\n- Support util: `.../utils/is-calendar-creation-supported-provider.util.ts`; scope util `.../utils/get-missing-create-event-scopes.util.ts` (Google `calendar.events`, Microsoft `Calendars.ReadWrite`)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Import / sync\n\n### 2a. Supported providers\n\n- Enum: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/types/ConnectedAccountProvider.ts` — `GOOGLE='google'`, `MICROSOFT='microsoft'`, `IMAP_SMTP_CALDAV='imap_smtp_caldav'`, plus `OIDC`, `SAML`, `EMAIL_GROUP`, `APP`.\n- Calendar sync dispatch supports exactly the first three:\n  - `.../calendar-event-import-manager/services/calendar-get-events.service.ts` (list fetch)\n  - `.../calendar-event-import-manager/services/calendar-import-events.service.ts` (detail fetch)\n  - Unsupported providers throw `PROVIDER_NOT_SUPPORTED`.\n\n### 2b. Import architecture & jobs\n\nModule: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-import-manager/calendar-event-import-manager.module.ts`\n\nPipeline (two-phase, pull only):\n1. **List fetch** (`CalendarFetchEventsService`) — `.../services/calendar-fetch-events.service.ts`\n   - Calls provider, gets `calendarEventIds`, `calendarEventIdsToDelete`, `nextSyncCursor`.\n   - Deletes associations + orphaned events for provider-side deletions, pushes ids into Redis set `calendar-events-to-import:{workspaceId}:{calendarChannelId}`, saves `syncCursor`.\n2. **Detail import** (`CalendarEventsImportService`) — `.../services/calendar-events-import.service.ts`\n   - Pops ids from cache in batches (`CALENDAR_EVENT_IMPORT_BATCH_SIZE`), fetches full events, filters cancelled/blocklisted (`filterEventsAndReturnCancelledEvents`), then persists in batches of 1000 via `CalendarSaveEventsService`.\n\nDriver list/import services:\n- Google: `.../drivers/google-calendar/services/google-calendar-get-events.service.ts` (`events.list` with `syncToken`, `showDeleted: true`, paginated) and `.../google-calendar-import-events.service.ts` (`events.get` per id).\n- Microsoft: `.../drivers/microsoft-calendar/services/microsoft-calendar-get-events.service.ts` (`/me/calendar/events/delta` + `PageIterator`, `@removed` → delete) and `.../microsoft-calendar-import-events.service.ts` (`/me/calendar/events/{id}`, Graph beta).\n- CalDAV: `.../drivers/caldav/services/caldav-get-events.service.ts`, `caldav-fetch-events.service.ts`, `caldav-import-events.service.ts`, `caldav-client.service.ts`, `providers/caldav-client.provider.ts`.\n\nCron/queue jobs (module providers list, lines 68–100):\n- `.../crons/jobs/calendar-event-list-fetch.cron.job.ts` — pattern `*/5 * * * *` (`CALENDAR_EVENT_LIST_FETCH_CRON_PATTERN`).\n- `.../crons/jobs/calendar-events-import.cron.job.ts` — pattern `*/1 * * * *`.\n- `.../crons/jobs/calendar-ongoing-stale.cron.job.ts` (stale-sync detection), `.../crons/jobs/calendar-relaunch-failed-calendar-channels.cron.job.ts`.\n- Job classes: `.../jobs/calendar-event-list-fetch.job.ts`, `calendar-events-import.job.ts`, `calendar-ongoing-stale.job.ts`, `calendar-relaunch-failed-calendar-channel.job.ts`.\n- Commands: `.../crons/commands/*.cron.command.ts`, `.../commands/calendar-trigger-event-list-fetch.command.ts`, `.../constants/calendar-ongoing-stale-sync-stages.constant.ts`, `.../constants/calendar-import-ongoing-sync-timeout.constant.ts`.\n- Queue used: `MessageQueue.calendarQueue` (+ `cronQueue`).\n\nReal-time import (push-triggered, but still a **pull** of event data):\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/connected-account-sync-webhooks/calendar-event-webhook-sync/services/calendar-event-webhook-sync.service.ts`\n  - On webhook, marks the channel fetch-scheduled, runs `CalendarFetchEventsService.fetchCalendarEvents`, then inline-imports or defers to cron (`CALENDAR_EVENT_WEBHOOK_SYNC_INLINE_IMPORT_MAX_EVENTS`, retry/timeout constants in same dir).\n- Webhook subscription drivers: `.../webhook-subscription-manager/drivers/google/google-webhook-subscription.driver.ts` (Google `watch`), `.../drivers/microsoft/microsoft-webhook-subscription.driver.ts` (resource `/me/events`), service `.../services/calendar-webhook-subscription.service.ts`, renewal cron `.../crons/jobs/webhook-subscription-renewal.cron.job.ts`.\n\n### 2c. Sync direction conclusion\n\n- **Provider → Twenty (pull):** full, for create (`insert`) / update (upsert by external id via `buildCalendarEventSaveOperations`) / delete (association removal + orphan cleanup). Incremental cursors: Google `syncToken`, Microsoft `deltaLink`, CalDAV sync-token/CTag.\n- **Twenty → provider (push):** **only create** (`events.insert` / Graph `POST /me/calendar/events` / CalDAV `createCalendarObject`). No update or delete push exists.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Provider-side write path search results\n\nSearched `createEvent`, `updateEvent`, `deleteEvent`, `insert`, `events().insert`, `graph.microsoft`, `CalendarEventsService`, `GoogleCalendarClient`, `MicrosoftCalendarClient`, `createCalendarObject`, `updateCalendarObject`, `deleteCalendarObject`.\n\n- **Create only**, as listed in 1e.\n- **No** `updateEvent` / `deleteEvent` / `events.patch` / `events.delete` / `updateCalendarObject` / `deleteCalendarObject` anywhere in `packages/twenty-server/src`.\n- No classes literally named `GoogleCalendarClient`/`MicrosoftCalendarClient` exist; clients are obtained inline from OAuth2 providers:\n  - `GoogleOAuth2ClientProvider` (`src/modules/connected-account/oauth2-client-manager/drivers/google/google-oauth2-client.provider`)\n  - `MicrosoftOAuth2ClientProvider` (`.../drivers/microsoft/microsoft-oauth2-client.provider`)\n  - `CalDavClientProvider` (`.../calendar-event-import-manager/drivers/caldav/providers/caldav-client.provider.ts`)\n- `CreateCalendarEventService` is the equivalent of a `CalendarEventsService` for writes; it only exposes `createComposedCalendarEvent` and `persistCalendarEvent`.\n\nConclusion: **no provider-side write path for local update/delete.** Local `calendarEvent` mutations (if done via API) never propagate outward; the next provider sync can overwrite them.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Connected accounts & calendar channel creation\n\n### 4a. Provider support\n\n- Providers with calendar sync/creation: **GOOGLE**, **MICROSOFT**, **IMAP_SMTP_CALDAV** (`ConnectedAccountProvider.ts`; `is-calendar-creation-supported-provider.util.ts`; front-end `isCalendarCreationEnabledForAccount.ts`).\n- Connected account entity: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/connected-account/entities/connected-account.entity.ts` — fields `provider` (line 55), `scopes` (76), encrypted `connectionParameters` (79, includes CALDAV), `calendarChannels` relation (127).\n\n### 4b. Channel creation on connection\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/auth/services/create-calendar-channel.service.ts`\n  - Creates `calendarChannel` with `connectedAccountId`, `handle`, `visibility` (default `METADATA`), and sync stage `PENDING_CONFIGURATION` (or `CALENDAR_EVENT_LIST_FETCH_PENDING` when skipping config).\n- Google OAuth connect: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/auth/services/google-apis.service.ts` (lines ~229–242, guarded by `isCalendarEnabled && isCalendarAvailable && existingCalendarChannels.length === 0`).\n- Microsoft OAuth connect: `.../auth/services/microsoft-apis.service.ts` (lines ~206–220, guarded by `CALENDAR_PROVIDER_MICROSOFT_ENABLED`).\n- CalDAV/IMAP connect: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/connected-account/services/imap-smtp-caldav-apis.service.ts` (lines ~116–157, creates channel only if `connectionParameters.CALDAV` present).\n- Kickoff: `.../connected-account/channel-sync/services/channel-sync.service.ts` (`startCalendarChannelSync`, lines 124–182) transitions `PENDING_CONFIGURATION` → `CALENDAR_EVENT_LIST_FETCH_SCHEDULED` and enqueues `CalendarEventListFetchJob` plus webhook subscription job.\n- Channel entity: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/calendar-channel/entities/calendar-channel.entity.ts` (core schema, `workspaceId`, `connectedAccountId`, `isSyncEnabled`, `syncCursor`, webhook subscription fields, visibility).\n\n### 4c. Provider capability signalling\n\n- Feature config (defaults **false**): `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/twenty-config/config-variables.ts` — `CALENDAR_PROVIDER_GOOGLE_ENABLED` (line 140), `CALENDAR_PROVIDER_MICROSOFT_ENABLED` (line 329).\n- Exposed to client: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/client-config/services/client-config.service.ts` (lines 275–283) as `isMicrosoftCalendarEnabled` / `isGoogleCalendarEnabled`.\n- OAuth scope signalling:\n  - Google scopes include `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events`: `.../auth/utils/get-google-apis-oauth-scopes.ts`\n  - Microsoft scopes include `Calendars.ReadWrite`: `.../auth/utils/get-microsoft-apis-oauth-scopes.ts`\n- Google Workspace service availability probe (Calendar API actually accessible): `.../auth/services/google-apis-service-availability.service.ts` (`checkCalendarAvailability`, returns `isCalendarAvailable`; guarded by `CALENDAR_PROVIDER_GOOGLE_ENABLED`).\n- Per-account create capability = granted scopes present: `get-missing-create-event-scopes.util.ts` (used by both server composer and front-end `hasMissingCreateCalendarEventScopes`).\n- Auth guards gate the OAuth flows on the config flags: `google-apis-oauth-request-code.guard.ts:62`, `google-apis-oauth-exchange-code-for-token.guard.ts:40`, `microsoft-apis-oauth-request-code.guard.ts:42`, `microsoft-apis-oauth-exchange-code-for-token.guard.ts:31`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. How `calendarEvent` records get workspace + connectedAccount linkage during import\n\nThere is **no `connectedAccountId` column on `calendarEvent`**. Linkage is indirect via the channel association junction:\n\n`calendarEvent` ← `calendarChannelEventAssociation.calendarEventId` → `calendarChannelId` → `calendarChannel.connectedAccountId` + `calendarChannel.workspaceId`.\n\n- Junction entity: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/standard-objects/calendar-channel-event-association.workspace-entity.ts` (`eventExternalId`, `recurringEventExternalId`, `calendarChannelId`, `calendarEventId`).\n- Save logic: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-import-manager/utils/build-calendar-event-save-operations.util.ts`\n  - If an association already exists for `eventExternalId` + `calendarChannelId`, updates the existing `calendarEvent` (by `calendarEventId`); otherwise generates a new `uuid` for the event and inserts event + association.\n- Persistence: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-import-manager/services/calendar-save-events.service.ts`\n  - Runs inside `workspaceOrmManager.executeInWorkspaceContext(buildSystemAuthContext(workspaceId))` and a workspace transaction; repositories are workspace-scoped so `workspaceId` is automatically added to queries and stamped on inserts (see `.../twenty-orm/workspace-scoped-repository/` — tests at `.../__tests__/workspace-scoped-repository.spec.ts` confirm `workspaceId` is merged into where and forced on entities).\n  - `connectedAccount` and `calendarChannel` are passed in explicitly from the import pipeline (`processCalendarEventsImport(calendarChannel, connectedAccount, workspaceId)`), so the channel carries the account linkage.\n  - Participants are written and matched afterwards (`CalendarEventParticipantService.matchParticipantsAndEnqueueContactCreationJob`), enabling Person/workspace-member links.\n- Visibility scoping: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/query-hooks/calendar-event/services/apply-calendar-events-visibility-restrictions.service.ts` resolves associations → channels → connected accounts to decide whether an event is visible, redacted (`FIELD_RESTRICTED_ADDITIONAL_PERMISSIONS_REQUIRED`), or removed. Hooks: `.../calendar-event-find-many.post-query.hook.ts`, `.../calendar-event-find-one.post-query.hook.ts`.\n\nFor the **creation** path, the same persistence mechanism is reused: `CreateCalendarEventService.persistCalendarEvent` calls `CalendarSaveEventsService.saveCalendarEventsAndEnqueueContactCreationJob([createdEvent], data.calendarChannel, data.connectedAccount, workspaceId)` (`create-calendar-event.service.ts:57–79`). So a locally created event is stored with its association to the chosen channel and is later reconciled by the import sync using its external id (Google event id / Graph event id / CalDAV href).\n\n---\n\n## Key takeaways\n\n1. **Manual creation exists** — via the calendar composer (`createCalendarEvent` metadata mutation), the `CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT` workflow action, and `CreateCalendarEventTool`. It is gated by `PermissionFlagType.CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT_TOOL`.\n2. The `calendarEvent` object is `isUICreatable: false` and every field `isUIEditable: false`; creation bypasses standard record CRUD.\n3. **Providers with create:** Google (`events.insert`), Microsoft Graph (`POST /me/calendar/events`), CalDAV (`createCalendarObject`).\n4. **Import/sync providers:** same three, with incremental cursors (Google `syncToken`, Microsoft delta, CalDAV sync-token/CTag) plus webhook-triggered pulls (Google watch, Microsoft subscriptions).\n5. **Update/delete push does not exist.** Only creation is written to providers; all other local changes are overwritten by the next pull.\n6. Linkage is `calendarEvent → calendarChannelEventAssociation → calendarChannel → connectedAccount` + `workspaceId` (enforced by the workspace-scoped ORM); no direct connected-account column on the event.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
