\n## 6. Navigation / menu item / \"calendar\" route\n\n- **No `AppPath.Calendar` and no `/calendar` route.** Calendar is created/selected as a **view type** on any object index page:\n  - View type selectable in `modules/object-record/object-options-dropdown/components/ObjectOptionsDropdownLayoutContent.tsx` (line 106: `setAndPersistViewType(ViewType.CALENDAR)`).\n  - `modules/views/view-picker/constants/ViewPickerTypeSelectOptions.ts` (line 19) and `ViewPickerContentCreateMode.tsx` (line 228, requires a date field).\n  - Label/icon: `modules/views/types/ViewType.ts` (`[ViewType.CALENDAR]: msg\\`Calendar\\``; `CALENDAR_WIDGET`: \"Calendar widget\").\n- **Navigation menu items are workspace-defined** (`modules/navigation-menu-item/`); there is **no hardcoded \"Calendar\" nav item**. `CoreObjectNameSingular.CalendarEvent = 'calendarEvent'` (`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/CoreObjectNameSingular.ts`) is a standard object with standard views (`allCalendarEvents` is a standard index view, not necessarily calendar type) — see `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object.constant.ts` lines 197–242.\n- **Record page \"Calendar\" tab/widget**: standard page layouts for Company/Person/Opportunity include a `calendar` tab rendering the calendar widget — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-page-layout-universal-identifiers.constant.ts` lines 88–93, 138–143, 189–194. Widget type config: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/types/page-layout/page-layout-widget-configuration.type.ts` (`CalendarConfiguration`, line 186).\n- **Command-menu / record action**: `useComposeCalendarEventRelatedRecordAction` (id `create-calendar-event`) surfaced through `useRelatedRecordActions.ts` (side panel \"Create related record\" flow, `SidePanelCreateRelatedRecordPage.tsx`) and the widget header action `getWidgetHeaderActionDefinition.ts` (`[WidgetType.CALENDAR]: WidgetActionCalendarEventCreate`).\n\n---\n\n## Summary answers\n\n1. **Is there a day/week/month calendar view, or only an event list/record page?** There is a full custom **Day/Week/Month record calendar grid** (`record-calendar`, `ViewCalendarLayout`), used for any object with a date field. Separately, calendar **events** are shown as a **month/day-grouped agenda list** (`activities/calendar`, the \"Calendar\" widget) and viewed through the generic record page/side panel. There is no `/calendar` route or standalone calendar page.\n2. **Which components render events/calendars?** Custom `RecordCalendarGrid`/`RecordCalendarGridDay`/`RecordCalendarCard` (grid) and `CalendarEventsCard`/`CalendarMonthCard`/`CalendarDayCardContent`/`CalendarEventRow` (agenda). **No FullCalendar.**\n3. **Create/edit/delete?** Create: yes (record calendar \"+\" per day, and calendar-event composer). Edit: generic inline field editing in the record calendar; drag to move records between days. Delete: only the generic record command menu. Calendar events themselves have **create only** — no update/delete/edit front-end mutations or forms; existing events open read-only-ish in the generic side-panel record page.\n4. **Settings:** `pages/settings/accounts/SettingsAccountsCalendars.tsx` (route `accounts/calendars`), channel details with visibility + contact auto-creation; `isSyncEnabled` is fetched but not exposed as a control there.\n5. **Recurrence:** none. **Attendees:** create-time guests + avatar display only. **Timezone:** user timezone, abbreviation, selectable timezone in composer and display settings.\n6. **Navigation/route:** no `AppPath.Calendar`; calendar is a `ViewType` and a page-layout widget/action; nav items are workspace-defined; related-record action id `create-calendar-event`.\n\nNo files were modified.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
