      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f4f7d0dcaffe3avRYijTgeeFuq\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed the research. Here is the factual report.\n\n---\n\n# Twenty app format: standard objects & permissions — findings\n\nAll paths are absolute. Working root: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite`.\n\n## 1. Application manifest/config format\n\n### `defineApplication` and `ApplicationConfig`\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/application/define-application.ts` — the `defineApplication` factory (validates `universalIdentifier`, `displayName`, variables, billing, configures logo/gallery).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/application/application-config.ts` — `ApplicationConfig` is literally `Omit<ApplicationManifest, ...>`. It is **not** a union with asset collections.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/application/applicationType.ts` — the real `ApplicationManifest` type.\n\nTop-level keys of the app config (`ApplicationManifest` + `SyncableEntityOptions`):\n\n`universalIdentifier`, `defaultRoleUniversalIdentifier` (deprecated), `displayName`, `description`, `applicationVariables`, `billing`, `serverVariables`, `author`, `category`, `logoUrl` (deprecated), `logo`, `screenshots` (deprecated), `galleryImages`, `aboutDescription`, `websiteUrl`, `termsUrl`, `emailSupport`, `issueReportUrl`, `postInstallLogicFunction`, `preInstallLogicFunction`, `uninstallLogicFunction`, `settingsFrontComponent`, `frontComponentSharedDependencies`, `settingsCustomTabFrontComponentUniversalIdentifier` (deprecated/ignored), `packageJsonChecksum`, `yarnLockChecksum`, `requiredServerVersionRange`.\n\nThe internal app configs are minimal examples of exactly this shape:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/real-estate/src/application.config.ts`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-projects/src/application.config.ts`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/application.config.ts`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-accounting/src/application.config.ts` (only app using `author`, `category`, `serverVariables`)\n\n### The keys you asked about (`objects`, `fields`, `frontComponents`, …) are NOT config keys\n\nThere is no `objects`, `fields`, `frontComponents`, `commandMenuItems`, `pageLayouts`, `logicFunctions`, `roles`, `permissions`, `navigationMenuItems`, or `searchProviders` key on `defineApplication` / `ApplicationConfig`. Assets are **separate files** each exporting a `define*()` default, discovered by scanning every `.ts`/`.tsx` in the app.\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/cli/utilities/build/manifest/manifest-extract-config.ts` — `TargetFunction` enum (`defineApplication`, `defineField`, `defineObject`, `defineRole`, `defineApplicationRole`, `defineView`, `defineNavigationMenuItem`, `definePageLayout`, `definePageLayoutTab`, `defineCommandMenuItem`, `defineLogicFunction`, `defineFrontComponent`, `defineAgent`, `defineSkill`, `defineConnectionProvider`, `definePermissionFlag`, `defineTimelineActivityType`, …) and `ManifestEntityKey` (the manifest collections).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/cli/utilities/build/manifest/manifest-build.ts` — `loadSources()` globs `**/*.ts`/`**/*.tsx` (lines 63–70), extracts the `define*` call per file, and assembles the manifest; single-role/hook constraints at lines 571–610. `loadAssets()` globs `${ASSETS_DIR}/**/*`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/application/manifestType.ts` — the final `Manifest` type. Its collections are: `application`, `objects`, `fields`, `indexes`, `logicFunctions`, `frontComponents`, `permissionFlags`, `roles`, `skills`, `agents`, `connectionProviders`, `publicAssets`, `views`, `viewFields`, `navigationMenuItems`, `pageLayouts`, `pageLayoutTabs`, `commandMenuItems`, `timelineActivityTypes`, `translations`. **There is no `searchProviders` collection.**\n\n### `searchProviders` — server-side only, not an app SDK concept\n\nThere is no `defineSearchProvider` in `packages/twenty-sdk`. Search providers are NestJS classes registered via a class decorator in server code:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/decorators/registered-search-provider.decorator.ts`\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/services/search-provider-registry.service.ts`\n- Example tied to the a2e-projects app by universal identifier: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/services/a2e-projects-search-provider.service.ts` (hardcodes `4f759655-84f8-434d-9c76-ee1850e8c1a4`, the a2e-projects manifest ID). It is registered in `search.module.ts`, not in the app.\n\n### Exports for defining assets\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/index.ts` is the public barrel (`twenty-sdk/define`). Relevant exports: `defineObject`, `defineField`, `STANDARD_OBJECT`/`STANDARD_OBJECT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS`, `defineRole`, `defineApplicationRole`, `definePermissionFlag`, `SystemPermissionFlag`, `defineView`, `defineViewField`, `defineNavigationMenuItem`, `definePageLayout`, `defineCommandMenuItem`, `defineLogicFunction`, `defineFrontComponent`, `defineAgent`, `defineSkill`, `defineConnectionProvider`, `defineIndex`, `defineTimelineActivityType`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Can an app extend a STANDARD object? — Yes, definitively\n\nThe SDK imposes no owner restriction. `FieldManifest` only requires an `objectUniversalIdentifier`, and the SDK exports the IDs of standard objects:\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/fields/define-field.ts` — validates only `objectUniversalIdentifier`, field validity.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/application/fieldManifestType.ts` — `objectUniversalIdentifier: string` (also `relationTargetObjectMetadataUniversalIdentifier` for relations).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/objects/standard-object-ids.ts` — re-exports `STANDARD_OBJECTS` as `STANDARD_OBJECT_UNIVERSAL_IDENTIFIERS` from `twenty-shared/metadata`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object.constant.ts` — the `STANDARD_OBJECTS` map (includes `calendarEvent`, `task`, `person`, `opportunity`, `company`, `note`, `workspaceMember`, …).\n\n### Internal apps that add fields to standard objects\n\n**real-estate** (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/real-estate/src/fields/`):\n- `person-budget-min.field.ts` — `CURRENCY` field on standard `person`.\n- `opportunity-buyer-stage.field.ts` — `SELECT` field on standard `opportunity`.\n- `buyer-on-opportunity.field.ts` — `RELATION` on standard `opportunity` → standard `person`.\n- `properties-for-sale-on-person.field.ts` — `RELATION` on standard `person` → **app-owned** `property`.\n- `seller-contact-on-property.field.ts`, `person-type.field.ts`, `person-desired-area.field.ts`, `person-pre-approved.field.ts`, `showings-on-person.field.ts`, `listed-properties-on-person.field.ts`, `buyer-opportunities-on-person.field.ts`, etc.\n\n**a2e-projects** (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-projects/src/fields/`):\n- `task-estimate.field.ts`, `task-priority.field.ts`, `task-human-id.field.ts`, `task-milestone.field.ts`, `task-project-status.field.ts`, `task-project.field.ts`, `task-subtasks.field.ts`, `task-time-entries.field.ts`, `task-labels.field.ts`, `task-estimate-label.field.ts`, `task-block-issue.field.ts` — all on standard `task` (and some on `note`).\n- `company-projects.field.ts` — relation on standard `company` → app `project`. The comment at lines 13–14: *\"Inverse of project.company, declared from the standard company side.\"*\n- `workspace-member-*.field.ts`, `lead-projects.field.ts`, `milestone-tasks.field.ts`, `project-tasks.field.ts` — standard `workspaceMember`/`company`/`task`.\n\n**a2e-accounting** (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-accounting/src/fields/`):\n- `company-invoices.field.ts` — standard `company` → app `invoice`; comment lines 5–6: *\"lives on the standard company object, which this app does not own — hence a standalone app-owned field manifest.\"*\n- `company-quotes.field.ts`, `opportunity-invoices.field.ts` (standard `opportunity`).\n\n**a2e-documents** (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/fields/`):\n- `person-documents.field.ts`, `company-documents.field.ts` — same pattern, standard `person`/`company`.\n\n**twenty-partners** (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/twenty-partners/src/modules/.../fields/`): standard `workspaceMember`/`opportunity`/`person`/`company`.\n\nPublic apps also do it: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/public/last-contact/src/fields/last-contact-for-opportunities-on-calendar-event.field.ts` (adds to standard `calendarEvent`), and `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/public/slack/src/fields/slack-user-links-on-workspace-member.field.ts` (standard `workspaceMember` → app object).\n\n### Server-side semantics of cross-app fields\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-manifest/converters/from-field-manifest-to-universal-flat-field-metadata.util.ts` — a field flat entity is stamped with `applicationUniversalIdentifier` = **the declaring app**, and `objectMetadataUniversalIdentifier` = the target object (the standard object). So the app owns the field; `twenty-standard` continues to own the object.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-manifest/services/compute-application-manifest-all-universal-flat-entity-maps.service.ts` — processes both `objectManifest.fields` and top-level `manifest.fields` (lines 77–125).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-manifest/application-manifest-migration.service.ts` (lines 124–131) — dependency maps always include the `twenty-standard` application so cross-app references resolve.\n- Engine also emits a visible view field on the standard object's INDEX view for such app fields: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/test/integration/metadata/suites/application/standard-object-index-view-field-manifest-sync.integration-spec.ts` (test description: *\"engine-emitted INDEX view field for an app field on a standard object\"*).\n- Apps can also extend another app's view with a view field: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/test/integration/metadata/suites/application/successful-sync-application-cross-app-view-field.integration-spec.ts`.\n- Standard objects cannot be deleted by non-standard apps: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/workspace-migration/workspace-migration-builder/validators/services/flat-object-metadata-validator.service.ts` (lines 157–166, `belongsToTwentyStandardApp` check); system objects cannot be updated directly (lines 63–76).\n\n**Answer: Yes** — an app can add a field, relation, or view field to a standard object (`calendarEvent`, `task`, `person`, …) and can add a relation from a standard object to an app-owned object. It owns the field it adds; it does not own the standard object.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Roles / permissions\n\n### SDK\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/roles/define-role.ts` — `defineRole`, validates `universalIdentifier`, `label`, object/field permission `objectUniversalIdentifier`, RLS predicate group/predicate references.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/roles/define-application-role.ts` — `defineApplicationRole` is a thin alias of `defineRole`. The CLI enforces **exactly one `defineApplicationRole` per app** (`manifest-build.ts` lines 591–593) and uses it as the app's default function role (lines 600–610). `defaultRoleUniversalIdentifier` on `defineApplication` is deprecated.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/roles/role-config.ts` — `RoleConfig` = `RoleManifest` minus the generated permission `universalIdentifier`s.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/application/roleManifestType.ts` — `RoleManifest`, `ObjectPermissionManifest`, `FieldPermissionManifest`, `RowLevelPermissionPredicateManifest`, `RowLevelPermissionPredicateGroupManifest`.\n\nA role declares:\n- Global booleans: `canUpdateAllSettings`, `canAccessAllTools`, `canReadAllObjectRecords`, `canUpdateAllObjectRecords`, `canSoftDeleteAllObjectRecords`, `canDestroyAllObjectRecords`, `canBeAssignedToUsers`, `canBeAssignedToAgents`, `canBeAssignedToApiKeys`.\n- `objectPermissions[]`: `{ objectUniversalIdentifier, canReadObjectRecords, canUpdateObjectRecords, canSoftDeleteObjectRecords, canDestroyObjectRecords }`.\n- `fieldPermissions[]`: `{ objectUniversalIdentifier, fieldUniversalIdentifier, canReadFieldValue, canUpdateFieldValue }`.\n- `rowLevelPermissionPredicates[]` / `rowLevelPermissionPredicateGroups[]`.\n- `permissionFlagUniversalIdentifiers[]`.\n\n### Yes — a role can grant access to standard objects\n\n`ObjectPermissionManifest.objectUniversalIdentifier` accepts any object ID, including standard ones. Concrete internal examples:\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/real-estate/src/roles/agent.role.ts` — `objectPermissions` on app `property`/`showing` **and** standard `person`, `note`, `task`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/twenty-partners/src/roles/partner.role.ts` — `objectPermissions` on app objects plus standard `opportunity`, `person`, `company`, `workspaceMember`; `fieldPermissions`; and `rowLevelPermissionPredicates` scoping standard `person`/`company`/`opportunity`/`workspaceMember` to the current member (`ownedByCurrentMember`, e.g. lines 591–665). Also `permissionFlagUniversalIdentifiers: [SystemPermissionFlag.UPLOAD_FILE]`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-accounting/src/roles/finance-user.role.ts` and `default-function.role.ts` — `fieldPermissions` denying `canReadFieldValue`/`canUpdateFieldValue` on app object `orgProfile.iban`/`bic` (source: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-accounting/src/lib/protected-bank-fields.ts`).\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-apps/internal/real-estate/src/roles/default-function.role.ts`, `a2e-projects/.../default-function.role.ts`, `a2e-documents/.../default-function.role.ts` — the app's `defineApplicationRole` (read/update/soft-delete all, not destroy).\n\n### Permission flags\n\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/permission-flags/define-permission-flag.ts` + `permission-flag-config.ts`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/roles/permission-flag-type.ts` re-exports `PermissionFlagType` as `PermissionFlag`.\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/constants/SystemPermissionFlag.ts` — built-in flags (`WORKSPACE`, `ROLES`, `DATA_MODEL`, `WORKFLOWS`, `APPLICATIONS`, `AI`, `UPLOAD_FILE`, …). These are system-wide feature grants, not per-object access.\n\n### Restrictions on roles\n\nAn app **cannot** attach permissions to another app's role, including the standard admin role:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/test/integration/metadata/suites/application/failing-sync-application-cross-app-permission-create-on-standard-role.integration-spec.ts` — adding a `permissionFlag`, `objectPermission`, or `fieldPermission` under `STANDARD_ROLE.admin` fails. Roles are app-owned; an app declares its own roles (role labels are workspace-globally unique, per the comment in the cross-app view-field spec).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Install / activation\n\n### Application entity\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application.entity.ts`:\n\n`id`, `universalIdentifier`, `name`, `description`, `logo`/`logoFileId`/`logoFile`, `version`, `sourceType`, `state`, `sourcePath`, `packageJsonChecksum`/`packageJsonFileId`, `yarnLockChecksum`/`yarnLockFileId`, `availablePackages`, `billing`, `logicFunctionLayerId`, `defaultRoleId`, `settingsCustomTabFrontComponentId`, `uninstallLogicFunctionId`, `uninstallHookCompletedForRequestedAt`, `canBeUninstalled`, `autoUpgrade`, `isSdkLayerStale`, `sdkClientCoreChecksum`, `frontComponentSharedDependenciesChecksum`/`BuiltPath`, `applicationRegistrationId`, `primaryPublicDomainId`, timestamps.\n\nThere is **no `isActive` / enabled / status field on the Application entity**. The lifecycle status is `state`:\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/enums/application-state.enum.ts`:\n`INSTALLING | INSTALLED | UPGRADING | UNINSTALLING`. (No `DISABLED`.)\n\n### What happens on install\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-install/application-install.service.ts`:\n\n- `installApplication` skips `LOCAL` and `OAUTH_ONLY` sources (lines 87–106), takes a cache lock, resolves the package.\n- `runInstall` (lines 232–434): workspace/version compatibility check, `ensureApplicationExists` (state `INSTALLING`), optional `UPGRADING`, `writeFilesToStorage`, `importLogoFile`, `runPreInstallHook`, `applyManifestToWorkspace`, `runPostInstallHook`, `refreshRegistrationFromManifest`, then `state = INSTALLED`. Failed fresh installs roll back via `applicationSyncService.uninstallApplication` (with uninstall hook disabled).\n\n`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-manifest/application-manifest-apply.service.ts` → `ApplicationSyncService.synchronizeFromManifest` (`.../application-manifest/application-sync.service.ts`) → `ApplicationManifestMigrationService.syncMetadataFromManifest` (`.../application-manifest/application-manifest-migration.service.ts`). It:\n- computes flat entities from the manifest (`compute-application-manifest-all-universal-flat-entity-maps.service.ts`), running a workspace migration for **all** manifest collections (objects, fields, indexes, roles, object/field permissions, RLS predicates/groups, views/view fields, nav items, page layouts/tabs/widgets, command menu items, logic functions, front components, agents, skills, connection providers, permission flags, timeline activity types, application variables),\n- generates the per-app SDK client,\n- syncs translations,\n- writes back app references: `defaultRoleId`, `settingsCustomTabFrontComponentId`, `uninstallLogicFunctionId` (lines 281–361),\n- on uninstall, deletes the app's metadata and refuses if data loss is detected (`ApplicationUninstallPreflightService`, `canBeUninstalled`).\n\n### \"Activation boundary\" (enabled/disabled, feature flags, per-workspace settings)\n\nThere is **no whole-app enable/disable toggle**. The boundaries that exist:\n\n1. **Install lifecycle state** — `ApplicationState` on the entity (above).\n2. **Per-workspace, per-entity activation (`isActive`) and overrides**, which survive app upgrades. `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-manifest/utils/preserve-application-local-metadata-state.util.ts` defines `APPLICATION_LOCAL_METADATA_PROPERTIES = ['overrides', 'universalOverrides', 'isActive']` and preserves them from the existing row when a manifest re-syncs. `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-manifest/utils/reconstruct-data-model-manifest.util.ts` marks a row deactivated in a workspace as `\"deactivated in this workspace, exported active\"`. So a workspace can deactivate an installed app's object/field/view/etc. while the app remains installed. Tests: `preserve-application-local-metadata-state.util.spec.ts`, `reconstruct-data-model-manifest.util.spec.ts`.\n3. **Global kill switch** (not per workspace): `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-stop/application-stop.service.ts` stores `kill-switch:<appUniversalIdentifier>` in cache; CLI `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-stop/commands/application-kill-switch.command.ts` (`application:kill-switch stop|remove`) halts the app's logic function executions on every workspace.\n4. **Feature flags** are workspace-level, not app-declared: `featureFlagsMap` is read during sync (e.g. `FeatureFlagKey.IS_LOGIC_FUNCTION_PREBUILT_MODE_ENABLED` in `application-manifest-migration.service.ts` lines 116–119).\n5. **Per-app settings/data**: `applicationVariables` + `serverVariables` (`ApplicationVariableEntity`, `serverVariables.type.ts`), app key-value store (`application-key-value/`), settings front component (`defineSettingsFrontComponent`), `canBeUninstalled`, `autoUpgrade`.\n6. Some individual entity kinds have their own `isActive` mutations (skills `activateSkill`/`deactivateSkill`, timeline activity types, command menu items) — but these are per-entity, not a per-app switch.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Can an app define/own an object named `calendarEvent`? — No\n\nIt cannot shadow a standard object; the name collides in the same workspace.\n\n- **Name-uniqueness (workspace-wide, any owner)** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/flat-object-metadata/validators/utils/validate-flat-object-metadata-name-and-labels.util.ts`, `doesOtherObjectWithSameNameExists` (lines 20–39): scans `universalFlatObjectMetadataMaps.byUniversalIdentifier` (which contains the standard objects from the `twenty-standard` app) and flags a match on `nameSingular`/`namePlural` regardless of owning application. On collision it raises `ObjectMetadataExceptionCode.OBJECT_ALREADY_EXISTS` / \"Object already exists\" (lines 80–97). The check runs across **both** singular/plural and cross singular/plural.\n- **DB uniqueness** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/object-metadata/object-metadata.entity.ts` lines 39–47: `@Unique` on `(nameSingular, workspaceId)` and `(namePlural, workspaceId)`.\n- **Reserved-keyword validator** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/flat-object-metadata/validators/utils/validate-flat-object-metadata-name.util.ts` + `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/reserved-metadata-name-keywords.constant.ts`. `calendarEvent` is **not** in the reserved-keyword list, so the operative guard is the name-collision check above; reserved names get an `INVALID_OBJECT_INPUT` error (UI path appends `Custom`, `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/utils/add-custom-suffix-if-reserved.util.ts`).\n- **Standard objects are twenty-standard-owned** — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/utils/belongs-to-twenty-standard-app.util.ts` compares against `TWENTY_STANDARD_APPLICATION.universalIdentifier = '20202020-64aa-4b6f-b003-9c74b97cee20'` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/application/constants/TwentyStandardApplicationUniversalIdentifier.ts`, `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/constants/twenty-standard-applications.ts`). Non-standard apps cannot delete standard objects (`flat-object-metadata-validator.service.ts` lines 157–166); direct update of system objects is limited to `overrides`/`isActive` (lines 63–76).\n\nSo: an app may **extend** `calendarEvent` (add fields, add relations from it), as `last-contact` does, but it may **not** create or own a `calendarEvent` object — the create fails with `OBJECT_ALREADY_EXISTS`, and even if it didn't, the standard object cannot be deleted or re-owned by a non-standard app.\n\n---\n\n## Quick reference — key files\n\n| Topic | Path |\n|---|---|\n| `defineApplication` + config type | `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/application/define-application.ts`, `.../application-config.ts` |\n| `ApplicationManifest` | `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/applicationType.ts` |\n| Full `Manifest` collections | `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/manifestType.ts` |\n| File discovery / entity kinds | `packages/twenty-sdk/src/cli/utilities/build/manifest/manifest-extract-config.ts`, `.../manifest-build.ts` |\n| SDK barrel | `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/index.ts` |\n| `defineField` / `FieldManifest` | `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/fields/define-field.ts`, `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/fieldManifestType.ts` |\n| Standard object IDs | `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/objects/standard-object-ids.ts`, `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object.constant.ts` |\n| `defineRole` / `RoleManifest` | `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/roles/define-role.ts`, `role-config.ts`, `packages/twenty-shared/src/application/roleManifestType.ts` |\n| `defineApplicationRole` | `packages/twenty-sdk/src/sdk/define/roles/define-application-role.ts` |\n| `SystemPermissionFlag` | `packages/twenty-shared/src/constants/SystemPermissionFlag.ts` |\n| Application entity / state | `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application.entity.ts`, `.../enums/application-state.enum.ts` |\n| Install flow | `.../application-install/application-install.service.ts` |\n| Manifest apply / sync / migration | `.../application-manifest/application-manifest-apply.service.ts`, `.../application-sync.service.ts`, `.../application-manifest-migration.service.ts` |\n| Cross-app field ownership | `.../application-manifest/converters/from-field-manifest-to-universal-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`, `.../services/compute-application-manifest-all-universal-flat-entity-maps.service.ts` |\n| Per-workspace `isActive` preservation | `.../application-manifest/utils/preserve-application-local-metadata-state.util.ts` |\n| Kill switch | `.../application-stop/application-stop.service.ts`, `.../application-stop/commands/application-kill-switch.command.ts` |\n| Object name collision | `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/flat-object-metadata/validators/utils/validate-flat-object-metadata-name-and-labels.util.ts` |\n| Standard-object deletion guard | `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/workspace-migration/workspace-migration-builder/validators/services/flat-object-metadata-validator.service.ts` |\n| Standard objects belong to standard app | `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/utils/belongs-to-twenty-standard-app.util.ts` |\n| Reserved names | `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/reserved-metadata-name-keywords.constant.ts` |\n| Search provider mechanism (server-only) | `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/search/decorators/registered-search-provider.decorator.ts`, `.../services/a2e-projects-search-provider.service.ts` |\n| Integration evidence: field on standard object | `packages/twenty-server/test/integration/metadata/suites/application/standard-object-index-view-field-manifest-sync.integration-spec.ts` |\n| Integration evidence: cross-app view field | `packages/twenty-server/test/integration/metadata/suites/application/successful-sync-application-cross-app-view-field.integration-spec.ts` |\n| Integration evidence: cross-app permission denied | `packages/twenty-server/test/integration/metadata/suites/application/failing-sync-application-cross-app-permission-create-on-standard-role.integration-spec.ts` |\n\nNo files were modified.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
