        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f4f80c36dffedteQKXLLNb41g5\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n# Calendar Standard Metadata in Twenty CRM — Factual Report\n\nAll paths are absolute. I did not modify anything.\n\n## 0. Where the metadata actually lives\n\nThere are three layers, and it matters which one you read:\n\n| Layer | Path | What it is |\n|---|---|---|\n| Standard metadata definitions (authoritative fields/types/nullability) | `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/field-metadata/compute-*-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts` | The real field metadata (`isNullable`, `type`, `defaultValue`, relations) |\n| Shared constants (object keys + deterministic universal identifiers) | `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object.constant.ts`, `standard-object-fields.constant.ts`, `standard-object-universal-identifiers.constant.ts` | Object registry, field IDs, indexes, views |\n| Runtime TypeScript workspace entities (slim, type-only) | `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/standard-objects/*.workspace-entity.ts` | ORM repository typing; does not carry all metadata |\n\nObject universal identifiers (`packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object-universal-identifiers.constant.ts:11-14`):\n- `calendarChannelEventAssociation`: `20202020-491b-4aaa-9825-afd1bae6ae00`\n- `calendarEvent`: `20202020-8f1d-4eef-9f85-0d1965e27221`\n- `calendarEventTarget`: `6a9b9656-3e23-4234-94a4-b913c5dde668`\n- `calendarEventParticipant`: `20202020-a1c3-47a6-9732-27e5b1e8436d`\n\nImportant finding: **`calendarChannel` is not a standard workspace object.** It is a core metadata entity (`core.calendarChannel`) and appears in `CoreObjectNameSingular` (`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/CoreObjectNameSingular.ts:7`) but is absent from `STANDARD_OBJECTS` in `standard-object.constant.ts` (only `calendarChannelEventAssociation`, `calendarEventParticipant`, `calendarEvent`, `calendarEventTarget` are there). The other three are standard objects of the workspace schema.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Standard objects and their files\n\n### `calendarEvent`\n- Runtime entity: `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/standard-objects/calendar-event.workspace-entity.ts`\n- Metadata: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/field-metadata/compute-calendar-event-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`\n- Object registration: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/object-metadata/create-standard-flat-object-metadata.util.ts:187-233` (`isSystem: true`, `isAuditLogged: false`, `isUICreatable: false`, label identifier `title`)\n- Shared fields: `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object-fields.constant.ts:298-346`\n\n### `calendarChannelEventAssociation`\n- Runtime entity: `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/standard-objects/calendar-channel-event-association.workspace-entity.ts`\n- Metadata: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/field-metadata/compute-calendar-channel-event-association-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`\n- Object registration: `create-standard-flat-object-metadata.util.ts:92-139` (`writability: MetadataWritability.SYSTEM`, `isAuditLogged: false`, label identifier `id`)\n- Indexes: `compute-calendar-channel-event-association-standard-flat-index-metadata.util.ts` (`calendarChannelIdIndex`), plus a `calendarEventIdIndex` declared in shared constants `standard-object.constant.ts:104-110`\n\n### `calendarEventParticipant`\n- Runtime entity: `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/standard-objects/calendar-event-participant.workspace-entity.ts`\n- Metadata: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/field-metadata/compute-calendar-event-participant-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`\n- Object registration: `create-standard-flat-object-metadata.util.ts:140-186` (label identifier `handle`)\n- Indexes: `calendarEventIdIndex`, `personIdIndex`, `workspaceMemberIdIndex` (`standard-object.constant.ts:147-157`)\n\n### `calendarEventTarget` (adjacent, referenced from calendarEvent)\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/standard-objects/calendar-event-target.workspace-entity.ts`\n- `compute-calendar-event-target-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`\n\n### `calendarChannel` (core entity, not a workspace object)\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/calendar-channel/entities/calendar-channel.entity.ts`\n- DTO: `.../calendar-channel/dtos/calendar-channel.dto.ts`\n- Resolver: `.../calendar-channel/resolvers/calendar-channel.resolver.ts`\n- Service: `.../calendar-channel/calendar-channel-metadata.service.ts`\n\n---\n\n## 2. `calendarEvent` — every field\n\nSource: `compute-calendar-event-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`. System fields `id, createdAt, updatedAt, deletedAt, createdBy, updatedBy, position, searchVector` are defined by `packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/utils/internal/build-standard-object-system-fields.util.ts:4-13`.\n\n| Field | Type | Nullable | Notes / line |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `id` | UUID | no | system, default `uuid`; L28 |\n| `createdAt` | DATE_TIME | no | system; L49 |\n| `updatedAt` | DATE_TIME | no | system; L73 |\n| `deletedAt` | DATE_TIME | yes | system; L100 |\n| `createdBy` | ACTOR | no | system; default `{source:'MANUAL', name:'System', workspaceMemberId:null}`; L126-155 |\n| `updatedBy` | ACTOR | no | system; same default; L156-185 |\n| `position` | POSITION | no | system, default `0`; L186 |\n| `searchVector` | TS_VECTOR | yes | system; L211 |\n| `title` | TEXT | yes | `isUIEditable:false`; L235 |\n| `isCanceled` | BOOLEAN | no | default `false`; L256 |\n| `isFullDay` | BOOLEAN | no | default `false`; L278 |\n| `startsAt` | DATE_TIME | yes | L300 |\n| `endsAt` | DATE_TIME | yes | L321 |\n| `externalCreatedAt` | DATE_TIME | yes | L342 |\n| `externalUpdatedAt` | DATE_TIME | yes | L366 |\n| `description` | TEXT | yes | `displayedMaxRows:99`; L390 |\n| `location` | TEXT | yes | L412 |\n| `iCalUid` | TEXT | yes | L433 |\n| `conferenceSolution` | TEXT | yes | L454 |\n| `conferenceLink` | LINKS | yes | `LinksMetadata`; L478 |\n| `calendarChannelEventAssociations` | RELATION (ONE_TO_MANY) | no | target `calendarChannelEventAssociation.calendarEvent`; L499 |\n| `calendarEventParticipants` | RELATION (ONE_TO_MANY) | no | target `calendarEventParticipant.calendarEvent`; L532 |\n| `calendarEventTargets` | RELATION (ONE_TO_MANY) | yes | target `calendarEventTarget.calendarEvent`; L565 |\n| `callRecordings` | RELATION (ONE_TO_MANY) | no | target `callRecording.calendarEvent`; L595 |\n\nNotes:\n- **No `recurrenceRule` field exists anywhere in the repo** (grep returned zero matches). Recurrence is represented only indirectly by `calendarChannelEventAssociation.recurringEventExternalId`.\n- The TypeScript workspace entity (`calendar-event.workspace-entity.ts:9-31`) declares a subset (`title, isCanceled, isFullDay, startsAt, endsAt, externalCreatedAt, externalUpdatedAt, description, location, iCalUid, conferenceSolution, conferenceLink`, plus the three reverse relations). `callRecordings` is deliberately omitted there with an explanatory comment (lines 29-31) though it exists in metadata.\n\n### Does it belong to a connected account or a workspace? How is the creator/owner represented?\n- It is a **workspace standard object**. There is no `workspaceId` column on it (verified against `STANDARD_OBJECT_SYSTEM_FIELD_NAMES`, which does not include `workspaceId`); scoping is by workspace schema/repository context.\n- It has **no `connectedAccountId`, no `ownerId`, and no `workspaceMemberId` field**. The connected account/ownership link is indirect: `calendarEvent` → `calendarChannelEventAssociation.calendarChannelId` → `core.calendarChannel.connectedAccountId` → `core.connectedAccount.userWorkspaceId`.\n- The only \"creator\" representation is the generic `createdBy` ACTOR field, whose default is `{ source: 'MANUAL', name: 'System', workspaceMemberId: null }` — i.e. not the connected-account owner. During import, `build-calendar-event-save-operations.util.ts:43-60` writes only content fields and never sets `createdBy`/`updatedBy`, so imported events keep the System default.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `calendarChannelEventAssociation`\n\nSource: `compute-calendar-channel-event-association-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`; entity `calendar-channel-event-association.workspace-entity.ts`.\n\n| Field | Type | Nullable | Notes / line |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `id` | UUID | no | L31 |\n| `createdAt`/`updatedAt` | DATE_TIME | no | L52/L76 |\n| `deletedAt` | DATE_TIME | yes | L103 |\n| `createdBy`/`updatedBy` | ACTOR | no | L129/L159 |\n| `position` | POSITION | no | default 0; L189 |\n| `searchVector` | TS_VECTOR | yes | L214 |\n| `eventExternalId` | TEXT | yes | provider event id; L238 |\n| `recurringEventExternalId` | TEXT | yes | recurring series id; L262 |\n| `calendarChannelId` | UUID | no | plain UUID, **not a relation** (channel is a core entity); L286-306 |\n| `calendarEvent` | RELATION (MANY_TO_ONE) | no | target `calendarEvent.calendarChannelEventAssociations`, `onDelete: CASCADE`, `joinColumnName: 'calendarEventId'`; L307-335 |\n\nRuntime entity confirms field shape at `calendar-channel-event-association.workspace-entity.ts:5-11`. Index on `calendarChannelId` (`compute-calendar-channel-event-association-standard-flat-index-metadata.util.ts:22-28`); a `calendarEventIdIndex` is also declared in `standard-object.constant.ts:108-110`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. `calendarEventParticipant`\n\nSource: `compute-calendar-event-participant-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`; entity `calendar-event-participant.workspace-entity.ts`.\n\n| Field | Type | Nullable | Notes / line |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `id`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `deletedAt`, `createdBy`, `updatedBy`, `position`, `searchVector` | system | — | L31-237 |\n| `handle` | TEXT | yes | email/handle; L238 |\n| `displayName` | TEXT | yes | L259 |\n| `isOrganizer` | BOOLEAN | no | default `false`; L280 |\n| `responseStatus` | SELECT | no | default `'NEEDS_ACTION'`; L302-364 |\n| `calendarEvent` | RELATION (MANY_TO_ONE) | no | target `calendarEvent.calendarEventParticipants`, `onDelete: CASCADE`, `joinColumnName: 'calendarEventId'`; L365-393 |\n| `person` | RELATION (MANY_TO_ONE) | yes | target `person.calendarEventParticipants`, `onDelete: SET_NULL`, `joinColumnName: 'personId'`; L394-422 |\n| `workspaceMember` | RELATION (MANY_TO_ONE) | yes | target `workspaceMember.calendarEventParticipants`, `onDelete: SET_NULL`, `joinColumnName: 'workspaceMemberId'`; L423-454 |\n\n`responseStatus` options (L321-358): `NEEDS_ACTION` (orange), `DECLINED` (red), `TENTATIVE` (yellow), `ACCEPTED` (green). The enum `CalendarEventParticipantResponseStatus` is declared in the runtime entity (`calendar-event-participant.workspace-entity.ts:7-12`).\n\nMatching to `person`/`workspaceMember` is asynchronous: `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-participant-manager/jobs/calendar-event-participant-match-participant.job.ts` calls `MatchParticipantService` for people (by email) and workspace members; listeners `calendar-event-participant-person.listener.ts` / `calendar-event-participant-workspace-member.listener.ts`.\n\nIndexes: `calendarEventIdIndex`, `personIdIndex`, `workspaceMemberIdIndex` (`standard-object.constant.ts:147-157`).\n\n---\n\n## 5. `calendarChannel`\n\nCore entity `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/calendar-channel/entities/calendar-channel.entity.ts`, table `core.calendarChannel` (L39). Extends `WorkspaceRelatedEntity`, which provides `workspaceId` (non-null) and a `workspace` relation (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/types/workspace-related-entity.ts:5-11`).\n\n| Property | Type | Nullable | Notes / line |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `id` | uuid | no | L51 |\n| `handle` | varchar | no | L54 |\n| `syncStatus` | enum `CalendarChannelSyncStatus` | no | default `NOT_SYNCED`; L57 |\n| `syncStage` | enum `CalendarChannelSyncStage` | no | L65 |\n| `visibility` | enum `CalendarChannelVisibility` | no | L72 |\n| `isContactAutoCreationEnabled` | boolean | no | default `true`; L79 |\n| `contactAutoCreationPolicy` | enum | no | default `AS_PARTICIPANT_AND_ORGANIZER`; L82 |\n| `isSyncEnabled` | boolean | no | default `true`; L91 |\n| `syncCursor` | varchar | yes | L94 |\n| `syncedAt` | timestamptz | yes | L97 |\n| `syncStageStartedAt` | timestamptz | yes | L100 |\n| `throttleFailureCount` | integer | no | default 0; L103 |\n| `webhookSubscriptionExternalId` | varchar | yes | L106 |\n| `webhookSubscriptionExternalResourceId` | varchar | yes | L109 |\n| `webhookSubscriptionClientState` | varchar | yes | L112 |\n| `webhookSubscriptionStatus` | enum | yes | L115 |\n| `webhookSubscriptionExpiresAt` | timestamptz | yes | L122 |\n| `connectedAccountId` | uuid | no | L125 |\n| `connectedAccount` | ManyToOne → `ConnectedAccountEntity`, `onDelete: CASCADE` | — | L128-134 |\n| `createdAt`/`updatedAt` | timestamptz | no | L136/L139 |\n\nRelation to connected account: `ConnectedAccountEntity.calendarChannels` is the inverse OneToMany (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/metadata-modules/connected-account/entities/connected-account.entity.ts:122-127`). The connected account carries `userWorkspaceId` (non-null, L87-88) and a `visibility: 'user' | 'workspace'` (L113-114), plus `archivedAt` (L69-70).\n\nEnums:\n- `CalendarChannelVisibility`: `METADATA`, `SHARE_EVERYTHING` (`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/CalendarChannelVisibility.ts`)\n- `CalendarChannelSyncStatus`: `NOT_SYNCED`, `ONGOING`, `ACTIVE`, `FAILED_INSUFFICIENT_PERMISSIONS`, `FAILED_UNKNOWN`\n- `CalendarChannelSyncStage`: `PENDING_CONFIGURATION`, `CALENDAR_EVENT_LIST_FETCH_PENDING/SCHEDULED/ONGOING`, `CALENDAR_EVENTS_IMPORT_PENDING/SCHEDULED/ONGOING`, `FAILED`\n- `CalendarChannelContactAutoCreationPolicy`: `AS_PARTICIPANT_AND_ORGANIZER`, `AS_PARTICIPANT`, `AS_ORGANIZER`, `NONE`\n\nDefault visibility on channel creation is **`METADATA`**: `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/auth/services/create-calendar-channel.service.ts:49`. GraphQL DTO exposes `handle, syncStatus, syncStage, visibility, isContactAutoCreationEnabled, contactAutoCreationPolicy, isSyncEnabled, syncedAt, syncStageStartedAt, throttleFailureCount, connectedAccountId, createdAt, updatedAt`; `syncCursor` and `workspaceId` are `@HideField` (`calendar-channel.dto.ts:62-85`). `updateCalendarChannel` can change `visibility`, `isContactAutoCreationEnabled`, `contactAutoCreationPolicy`, `isSyncEnabled` (`update-calendar-channel.input.ts:19-40`).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Workspace-scoped vs creator-scoped: per-user visibility filtering\n\n**Storage is workspace-scoped, but reads are filtered per-user.** There is no owner column on `calendarEvent`; instead a GraphQL post-query hook rewrites/removes results based on channel visibility and whether the current user owns the connected account.\n\nKey files:\n- `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/query-hooks/calendar-event/calendar-event-find-many.post-query.hook.ts` — registered for key `calendarEvent.findMany` (L13-16), extracts `userId` only for user auth contexts (L27-28), calls the visibility service (L47-51).\n- `.../calendar-event/calendar-event-find-one.post-query.hook.ts` — same for `calendarEvent.findOne` (L13-16, L47-51).\n- `.../calendar-event/services/apply-calendar-events-visibility-restrictions.service.ts` — the actual algorithm.\n- Wiring: `.../calendar-query-hook.module.ts` (providers L21-27; TypeORM repositories `CalendarChannelEntity`, `ConnectedAccountEntity`, `UserWorkspaceEntity` L15-19).\n\nAlgorithm (`apply-calendar-events-visibility-restrictions.service.ts:30-142`):\n1. Fetch associations for the returned events (L44-49), collect `calendarChannelId`s (L51-57), load `core.calendarChannel` rows for the workspace (L59-67).\n2. For each event, group its channels by `visibility` (L85-88).\n3. If any channel is `SHARE_EVERYTHING` → keep event fully (L90-96).\n4. If a user context exists, resolve the user's `userWorkspace` (L98-102) and look for a `ConnectedAccount` whose `calendarChannels.id` is among the event's channels and whose `userWorkspaceId` matches → if found, keep event fully (L104-120). This is the per-user ownership check (owner of the connected account).\n5. Else if any channel is `METADATA` → set `title` and `description` to `FIELD_RESTRICTED_ADDITIONAL_PERMISSIONS_REQUIRED` (L122-132).\n6. Otherwise `splice` the event out of the payload (L134).\n\nBecause `CalendarChannelVisibility` has only `METADATA` and `SHARE_EVERYTHING`, the effective behavior is:\n- `SHARE_EVERYTHING` → every workspace user sees the full event.\n- `METADATA` (the default) → the connected-account owner sees the full event; other workspace users get the event with `title`/`description` redacted.\n- Events whose associations reference no channel / unknown channel are dropped (step 6).\n\nThe same ownership+visibility logic is reimplemented for the timeline API in `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/calendar/timeline-calendar-event.service.ts:208-315`: it resolves the current user's `userWorkspaceId`, computes `ownedAccountIds`, and sets `hasFullAccess = visibility === 'SHARE_EVERYTHING' || isOwnedByCurrentUser` (L286-301), redacting title/description otherwise (L308-315).\n\nAdditional per-user scoping:\n- `myCalendarChannels` only returns channels for the caller's connected accounts: resolver `calendar-channel.resolver.ts:24-49` → `CalendarChannelMetadataService.findByUserWorkspaceId` → `getUserConnectedAccountIds` (`calendar-channel-metadata.service.ts:35-52`).\n- `updateCalendarChannel` and `findByConnectedAccountIdForUser` enforce ownership via `verifyOwnership` (`calendar-channel-metadata.service.ts:110-144`), which throws `CALENDAR_CHANNEL_OWNERSHIP_VIOLATION` if the channel's `connectedAccountId` is not among the user's connected accounts.\n- `createCalendarEvent` verifies connected-account ownership before composing/creating: `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-creation-manager/resolvers/create-calendar-event.resolver.ts:49-53`, guarded by `SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT_TOOL)` (L29-32). Blank `connectedAccountId` falls back to the oldest sync-enabled channel in the workspace (`calendar-event-composer.service.ts:189-261`).\n\nThere is **no calendar-event–specific read resolver** in `packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar`; the only resolver there is `create-calendar-event.resolver.ts`. Reads go through the generic workspace GraphQL query runner and are intercepted by the two post-query hooks above.\n\n### Summary\n- `calendarEvent` is stored workspace-wide, with no owner/connected-account column.\n- Visibility is enforced at read time per user via the association → channel → connected account → userWorkspace chain.\n- Default channel visibility is `METADATA` (owner full, others redacted title/description); `SHARE_EVERYTHING` exposes full events to the whole workspace.\n- `createdBy`/`updatedBy` are generic ACTOR fields defaulting to `System` and are not used as an ownership filter.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
