        "result": "<task id=\"ses_f4f80bbb5ffeR83kqFvhtIZaEU\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have completed a thorough investigation. Here is the factual report.\n\n---\n\n# Calendar Event Creation & Sync in Twenty CRM — Research Report\n\n## Executive summary\n\nThe premise that events are **only imported** is **not true in this repo**. There is a fully implemented, wired provider-side **creation** path (manual UI composer + workflow action + AI/action tool + metadata GraphQL mutation) that writes events to Google, Microsoft Graph, and CalDAV. However, **update and delete are import-only**: no code path pushes a local edit or deletion back to any provider. So overall it is **bidirectional for create, one-way (pull) for update/delete**.\n\nThe calendar event object itself is deliberately **not UI-editable / not UI-creatable**; creation is done through a dedicated composer that calls a custom metadata mutation, not the standard record CRUD.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Creation drivers for `calendarEvent`\n\n### 1a. Object metadata flags — the standard UI cannot create/edit these records\n\n`calendarEvent` object metadata:\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/object-metadata/create-standard-flat-object-metadata.util.ts` (lines 187–233)\n  - `isSystem: true`, `isUICreatable: false`, `openRecordIn: SIDE_PANEL`.\n\nAll fields are `isUIEditable: false` (the current name; `isUIReadOnly` is the deprecated inverted alias — see `from-flat-field-metadata-to-field-metadata-dto.util.ts:47` and `from-object-metadata-entity-to-object-metadata-dto.util.ts:24`):\n- `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/workspace-manager/twenty-standard-application/utils/field-metadata/compute-calendar-event-standard-flat-field-metadata.util.ts`\n  - `title` (249), `isCanceled` (270), `isFullDay` (292), `startsAt` (314), `endsAt` (335), `externalCreatedAt` (359), `externalUpdatedAt` (383), `description` (404), `location` (426), `iCalUid` (447), `conferenceSolution` (471), `conferenceLink` (492), relations, etc. — all `false`.\n- Workspace entity (TS shape): `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/standard-objects/calendar-event.workspace-entity.ts`\n- Deprecation/migration note: `.../upgrade-version-command/2-13/2-13-instance-command-fast-1781277453604-rename-is-ui-read-only-to-is-ui-editable.ts`\n\nConsequence: the generic \"create record\" UI and inline field editing are disabled. The data API (`createOne`/`createMany`) is not blocked by a hook for `calendarEvent` (only find hooks exist), but the UI does not expose it.\n\n### 1b. Manual creation in the app — YES, via a dedicated composer\n\nFront-end module: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/calendar/`\n\n- Mutation document: `.../graphql/mutations/createCalendarEvent.ts` (`mutation CreateCalendarEvent($input: CreateCalendarEventInput!)`)\n- Apollo hook: `.../hooks/useCreateCalendarEvent.ts`\n- State machine/handler: `.../hooks/useCalendarEventComposer.ts` (calls `createCalendarEvent`, then links related records via `createCalendarEventTargets`)\n- UI fields: `.../components/CalendarEventComposerFields.tsx`\n- Entry point on records: `.../hooks/useComposeCalendarEventRelatedRecordAction.ts` (\"Create calendar event\" action, gated on `PermissionFlagType.CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT_TOOL`)\n- Account eligibility: `.../utils/isCalendarCreationEnabledForAccount.ts` (Google / Microsoft / IMAP_SMTP_CALDAV only, must have a sync-enabled channel)\n- Side-panel opener: `.../hooks/useComposeCalendarEventForTargetRecord.ts` and `@/side-panel/hooks/useOpenComposeCalendarEventInSidePanel`\n\n### 1c. Server-side create resolver and service\n\n- Resolver: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-creation-manager/resolvers/create-calendar-event.resolver.ts`\n  - `@MetadataResolver()`, `WorkspaceAuthGuard` + `SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT_TOOL)`.\n  - Verifies connected-account ownership, composes, creates at the provider, then persists locally.\n- Module wiring: `.../create-calendar-event.module.ts` → imported by\n  `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/core-engine.module.ts` (lines 83, 144).\n- DTOs: `.../dtos/create-calendar-event.input.ts` (`connectedAccountId`, `title`, `description`, `location`, `startsAt`, `endsAt`, `isFullDay`, `timeZone`, comma-separated `attendees`, `sendInvitations`, `addConferencing`), `.../dtos/create-calendar-event-output.dto.ts`.\n- Permission flag: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/constants/PermissionFlagType.ts:22`, definition in `.../permission-flag/constants/standard-permission-flag-definitions.constant.ts:122` (\"Create calendar events via connected accounts\"), tool list in `.../permissions/constants/tool-permission-flags.ts:7`.\n\n### 1d. Other creation drivers\n\n- **Workflow action** `CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT`:\n  - `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/workflow/workflow-executor/workflow-actions/create-calendar-event/create-calendar-event.workflow-action.ts`\n  - Registered in `.../factories/workflow-action.factory.ts:64`; type in `.../workflow-actions/types/workflow-action.type.ts:58`; builder in `.../workflow-builder/workflow-version-step/workflow-version-step-operations.workspace-service.ts:355`.\n- **Tool** `CreateCalendarEventTool` (also used by AI agents / action tools):\n  - `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/tool/tools/calendar-tool/create-calendar-event-tool.ts`\n  - Schema/types: `.../calendar-tool/calendar-tool.schema.ts`, `.../calendar-tool/types/create-calendar-event-tool-input.type.ts`\n  - Registered in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/tool/to