rs.ReadWrite`: `.../auth/utils/get-microsoft-apis-oauth-scopes.ts`\n- Google Workspace service availability probe (Calendar API actually accessible): `.../auth/services/google-apis-service-availability.service.ts` (`checkCalendarAvailability`, returns `isCalendarAvailable`; guarded by `CALENDAR_PROVIDER_GOOGLE_ENABLED`).\n- Per-account create capability = granted scopes present: `get-missing-create-event-scopes.util.ts` (used by both server composer and front-end `hasMissingCreateCalendarEventScopes`).\n- Auth guards gate the OAuth flows on the config flags: `google-apis-oauth-request-code.guard.ts:62`, `google-apis-oauth-exchange-code-for-token.guard.ts:40`, `microsoft-apis-oauth-request-code.guard.ts:42`, `microsoft-apis-oauth-exchange-code-for-token.guard.ts:31`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. How `calendarEvent` records get workspace + connectedAccount linkage during import\n\nThere is **no `connectedAccountId` column on `calendarEvent`**. Linkage is indirect via the channel association junction:\n\n`calendarEvent` ← `calendarChannelEventAssociation.calendarEventId` → `calendarChannelId` → `calendarChannel.connectedAccountId` + `calendarChannel.workspaceId`.\n\n- Junction entity: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/standard-objects/calendar-channel-event-association.workspace-entity.ts` (`eventExternalId`, `recurringEventExternalId`, `calendarChannelId`, `calendarEventId`).\n- Save logic: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-import-manager/utils/build-calendar-event-save-operations.util.ts`\n  - If an association already exists for `eventExternalId` + `calendarChannelId`, updates the existing `calendarEvent` (by `calendarEventId`); otherwise generates a new `uuid` for the event and inserts event + association.\n- Persistence: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/calendar-event-import-manager/services/calendar-save-events.service.ts`\n  - Runs inside `workspaceOrmManager.executeInWorkspaceContext(buildSystemAuthContext(workspaceId))` and a workspace transaction; repositories are workspace-scoped so `workspaceId` is automatically added to queries and stamped on inserts (see `.../twenty-orm/workspace-scoped-repository/` — tests at `.../__tests__/workspace-scoped-repository.spec.ts` confirm `workspaceId` is merged into where and forced on entities).\n  - `connectedAccount` and `calendarChannel` are passed in explicitly from the import pipeline (`processCalendarEventsImport(calendarChannel, connectedAccount, workspaceId)`), so the channel carries the account linkage.\n  - Participants are written and matched afterwards (`CalendarEventParticipantService.matchParticipantsAndEnqueueContactCreationJob`), enabling Person/workspace-member links.\n- Visibility scoping: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/query-hooks/calendar-event/services/apply-calendar-events-visibility-restrictions.service.ts` resolves associations → channels → connected accounts to decide whether an event is visible, redacted (`FIELD_RESTRICTED_ADDITIONAL_PERMISSIONS_REQUIRED`), or removed. Hooks: `.../calendar-event-find-many.post-query.hook.ts`, `.../calendar-event-find-one.post-query.hook.ts`.\n\nFor the **creation** path, the same persistence mechanism is reused: `CreateCalendarEventService.persistCalendarEvent` calls `CalendarSaveEventsService.saveCalendarEventsAndEnqueueContactCreationJob([createdEvent], data.calendarChannel, data.connectedAccount, workspaceId)` (`create-calendar-event.service.ts:57–79`). So a locally created event is stored with its association to the chosen channel and is later reconciled by the import sync using its external id (Google event id / Graph event id / CalDAV href).\n\n---\n\n## Key takeaways\n\n1. **Manual creation exists** — via the calendar composer (`createCalendarEvent` metadata mutation), the `CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT` workflow action, and `CreateCalendarEventTool`. It is gated by `PermissionFlagType.CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT_TOOL`.\n2. The `calendarEvent` object is `isUICreatable: false` and every field `isUIEditable: false`; creation bypasses standard record CRUD.\n3. **Providers with create:** Google (`events.insert`), Microsoft Graph (`POST /me/calendar/events`), CalDAV (`createCalendarObject`).\n4. **Import/sync providers:** same three, with incremental cursors (Google `syncToken`, Microsoft delta, CalDAV sync-token/CTag) plus webhook-triggered pulls (Google watch, Microsoft subscriptions).\n5. **Update/delete push does not exist.** Only creation is written to providers; all other local changes are overwritten by the next pull.\n6. Linkage is `calendarEvent → calendarChannelEventAssociation → calendarChannel → connectedAccount` + `workspaceId` (enforced by the workspace-scoped ORM); no direct connected-account column on the event.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
