EventNotSharedContent.tsx` (shown when channel visibility is metadata-only)\n- `CalendarEventComposerFields.tsx`, `CalendarEventComposerTargetsInput.tsx`, `CalendarEventLocationInput.tsx`\n- Types/context: `modules/activities/calendar/types/CalendarEvent.ts`, `contexts/CalendarContext.ts`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Create / edit / delete capabilities\n\n### Generic record calendar (any object)\n- **Create**: yes, but via a hover \"+\" button in a day cell, not drag-to-create.\n  - `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-calendar/components/RecordCalendarAddNew.tsx` (calls `createNewIndexRecord`, seeds the calendar date field).\n- **Edit**: yes, inline per-field editing.\n  - `RecordCalendarCardBody.tsx` wires `FieldContext` + `RecordInlineCell` with `updateOneRecord`.\n  - Edit/hover portals: `.../record-calendar-card/anchored-portal/components/RecordCalendarCardCellEditModePortal.tsx`, `RecordCalendarCardCellHoveredPortal.tsx`.\n- **Move**: drag-and-drop between day cells (moves the record's date/datetime; no resize/edge-drag, no drag-to-create).\n  - `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-calendar/hooks/useRecordCalendarDndKit.ts`\n  - `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/object-record/record-drag/hooks/useProcessCalendarCardDrop.ts` (calls `updateOneRecord`, shifts date/datetime).\n  - Date-shift utils: `modules/object-record/record-drag/utils/getShiftedRecordCalendar{Date,DateTime,DateUpdateInput,DateTimeUpdateInput}.ts`\n- **Delete**: no calendar-specific delete; right-click opens the generic record-index command menu (`RecordCalendarCard.tsx` `handleContextMenuOpen` → `commandMenuId`).\n- **Read-only guards**: `modules/object-record/record-calendar/states/isRecordCalendarReadOnlyComponentState.ts`, `record-calendar-widget/components/RecordCalendarWidgetReadOnlyEffect.tsx`, `record-calendar-card/hooks/useIsRecordCalendarCardDragDisabled.ts`.\n\nImportant: this calendar is **object-agnostic** — it renders any object's records by a chosen date field (`isFieldMetadataItemAvailableAsCalendarField`), so it is not specific to `calendarEvent`. Available date fields: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/views/view-picker/hooks/useGetAvailableFieldsForCalendar.ts`.\n\n### Calendar events (`activities/calendar`)\n- **Create only** (from a related record). No update/delete/editing UI.\n  - Composer state/hook: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/calendar/hooks/useCalendarEventComposer.ts`\n  - Mutation hook: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/calendar/hooks/useCreateCalendarEvent.ts`\n  - GraphQL: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/calendar/graphql/mutations/createCalendarEvent.ts` (`createCalendarEvent`)\n  - Side-panel page: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/pages/compose-calendar-event/components/SidePanelComposeCalendarEventPage.tsx`\n  - Opener: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/hooks/useOpenComposeCalendarEventInSidePanel.ts`\n  - Related-record action (id `create-calendar-event`): `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/calendar/hooks/useComposeCalendarEventRelatedRecordAction.ts`, registered in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/hooks/useRelatedRecordActions.ts`\n  - Widget header action: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/page-layout/widgets/calendar/components/WidgetActionCalendarEventCreate.tsx`\n  - Workflow action (automation, not interactive): `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/workflow/workflow-steps/workflow-actions/constants/actions/CreateCalendarEventAction.ts` (`CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT`) with `WorkflowEditActionCreateCalendarEvent.tsx`.\n- **Viewing an existing event**: opens the generic record in the side panel.\n  - `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/side-panel/hooks/useOpenCalendarEventInSidePanel.ts`\n  - `CalendarEventRow.tsx` calls it on click (only when `visibility === SHARE_EVERYTHING`).\n- **No front-end `updateCalendarEvent` / `deleteCalendarEvent`** mutations exist (searched; only `CREATE_CALENDAR_EVENT` under `activities/calendar/graphql/mutations/`). There is also no edit/delete control in `CalendarEventRow` or the calendar widget.\n- The create payload confirms the supported fields: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts` lines 1218–1230 (`CreateCalendarEventInput`: `title`, `description`, `location`, `startsAt`, `endsAt`, `isFullDay`, `timeZone`, `attendees`, `sendInvitations`, `addConferencing`, `connectedAccountId`) — **no recurrence field**.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Calendar settings (connected accounts / channels)\n\nRoute constant: `SettingsPath.AccountsCalendars = 'accounts/calendars'` in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/types/SettingsPath.ts` (line 8).\n\n- Route registration: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/app/components/SettingsRoutes.tsx` (lazy import lines 435–438; `<Route path={SettingsPath.AccountsCalendars} element={<SettingsAccountsCalendars />} />` lines 731–732).\n- Settings nav item (\"Accounts → Calendars\", `IconCalendarEvent`): `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/hooks/useSettingsNavigationItems.tsx` lines 106–112.\n- Page: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/accounts/SettingsAccountsCalendars.tsx`\n- Configuration step: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/pages/settings/accounts/SettingsAccountsConfigurationStepCalendar.tsx`\n\nComponents under `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/accounts/components/`:\n- `SettingsAccountsCalendarChannelsContainer.tsx` (tab per channel)\n- `SettingsAccountsCalendarChannelDetails.tsx` — **Event visibility** + **Contact auto-creation** toggles. It calls `UPDATE_CALENDAR_CHANNEL` (`{ visibility, isContactAutoCreationEnabled }`). The prop type includes `isSyncEnabled`, but the component does **not render a sync/enable toggle** (the field is fetched only).\n- `SettingsAccountsCalendarVisibilitySettingsCard.tsx` (exported as `SettingsAccountsEventVisibilitySettingsCard`) — options `CalendarChannelVisibility.SHARE_EVERYTHING` (\"Everything\") / `METADATA` (\"Metadata\").\n- `SettingsAccountsCalendarDisplaySettings.tsx` — time zone, date format, time format selects.\n- Mutation: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/accounts/graphql/mutations/updateCalendarChannel.ts`\n- Query: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/accounts/graphql/queries/getMyCalendarChannels.ts`\n- Hook: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/accounts/hooks/useMyCalendarChannels.ts`\n- Channel type: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/accounts/types/CalendarChannel.ts`\n- Account-level sync status display: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/accounts/components/SettingsAccountsConnectedAccountsRowRightContainer.tsx`\n- CalDAV connection form mentions calendar sync: `SettingsAccountsConnectionForm.tsx` (lines ~328–329).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Recurrence / attendee / timezone handling\n\n### Recurrence\n- **No recurrence UI anywhere** (searched `recurrence|recurring|RRULE` in `activities/calendar` → none). No \"repeat\" picker in the composer.\n- Recurrence exists only server-side as sync metadata: `recurringEventExternalId` on `calendarChannelEventAssociation` (`/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object-fields.constant.ts` line 268; `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-server/src/modules/calendar/common/standard-objects/calendar-channel-event-association.workspace-entity.ts`). The `CalendarEvent` entity itself has no recurrence field (`.../calendar-event.workspace-entity.ts`).\n\n### Attendees / guests\n- Create-time only: \"Guests\" row in `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/calendar/components/CalendarEventComposerFields.tsx` (uses `EmailRecipientsFieldInput`), plus related-record targets input `CalendarEventComposerTargetsInput.tsx`.\n- Display: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/activities/calendar/components/CalendarEventParticipantsAvatarGroup.tsx`.\n- Participant type: `modules/activities/calendar/types/CalendarEventParticipant.ts`; server object `calendarEventParticipant` (`calendarEventParticipant.workspace-entity.ts`, standard-object-fields.constant.ts lines 272–297 with `isOrganizer`, `responseStatus`).\n- No attendee management UI on an existing event.\n\n### Timezone\n- Hook: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ui/input/components/internal/date/hooks/useUserTimezone.ts`\n- Display: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/ui/input/components/internal/date/components/TimeZoneAbbreviation.tsx` (used in `RecordCalendarTopBar.tsx` line 200).\n- Options: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-front/src/modules/settings/experience/constants/AvailableTimezoneOptions.ts`\n- Composer \"Time zone\" select: `CalendarEventComposerFields.tsx` lines 233–246; date/time inputs `FormDateFieldInput` / `FormDateTimeFieldInput` receive `timeZone`.\n- Calendar view uses `Temporal` (`temporal-polyfill`) and shifts plain dates into the user's timezone (e.g. `RecordCalendarGridDay.tsx`, `useRecordCalendarQueryDateRangeFilter.tsx`).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Navigation / menu item / \"calendar\" route\n\n- **No `AppPath.Calendar` and no `/calendar` route.** Calendar is created/selected as a **view type** on any object index page:\n  - View type selectable in `modules/object-record/object-options-dropdown/components/ObjectOptionsDropdownLayoutContent.tsx` (line 106: `setAndPersistViewType(ViewType.CALENDAR)`).\n  - `modules/views/view-picker/constants/ViewPickerTypeSelectOptions.ts` (line 19) and `ViewPickerContentCreateMode.tsx` (line 228, requires a date field).\n  - Label/icon: `modules/views/types/ViewType.ts` (`[ViewType.CALENDAR]: msg\\`Calendar\\``; `CALENDAR_WIDGET`: \"Calendar widget\").\n- **Navigation menu items are workspace-defined** (`modules/navigation-menu-item/`); there is **no hardcoded \"Calendar\" nav item**. `CoreObjectNameSingular.CalendarEvent = 'calendarEvent'` (`packages/twenty-shared/src/types/CoreObjectNameSingular.ts`) is a standard object with standard views (`allCalendarEvents` is a standard index view, not necessarily calendar type) — see `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-object.constant.ts` lines 197–242.\n- **Record page \"Calendar\" tab/widget**: standard page layouts for Company/Person/Opportunity include a `calendar` tab rendering the calendar widget — `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/metadata/constants/standard-page-layout-universal-identifiers.constant.ts` lines 88–93, 138–143, 189–194. Widget type config: `/Users/maxaubert/Projets/A2E Suite/packages/twenty-shared/src/types/page-layout/page-layout-widget-configuration.type.ts` (`CalendarConfiguration`, line 186).\n- **Command-menu / record action**: `useComposeCalendarEventRelatedRecordAction` (id `create-calendar-event`) surfaced through `useRelatedRecordActions.ts` (side panel \"Create related record\" flow, `SidePanelCreateRelatedRecordPage.tsx`) and the widget header action `getWidgetHeaderActionDefinition.ts` (`[WidgetType.CALENDAR]: WidgetActionCalendarEventCreate`).\n\n---\n\n## Summary answers\n\n1. **Is there a day/week/month calendar view, or only an event list/record page?** There is a full custom **Day/Week/Month record calendar grid** (`record-calendar`, `ViewCalendarLayout`), used for any object with a date field. Separately, calendar **events** are shown as a **month/day-grouped agenda list** (`activities/calendar`, the \"Calendar\" widget) and viewed through the generic record page/side panel. There is no `/calendar` route or standalone calendar page.\n2. **Which components render events/calendars?** Custom `RecordCalendarGrid`/`RecordCalendarGridDay`/`RecordCalendarCard` (grid) and `CalendarEventsCard`/`CalendarMonthCard`/`CalendarDayCardContent`/`CalendarEventRow` (agenda). **No FullCalendar.**\n3. **Create/edit/delete?** Create: yes (record calendar \"+\" per day, and calendar-event composer). Edit: generic inline field editing in the record calendar; drag to move records between days. Delete: only the generic record command menu. Calendar events themselves have **create only** — no update/delete/edit front-end mutations or forms; existing events open read-only-ish in the generic side-panel record page.\n4. **Settings:** `pages/settings/accounts/SettingsAccountsCalendars.tsx` (route `accounts/calendars`), channel details with visibility + contact auto-creation; `isSyncEnabled` is fetched but not exposed as a control there.\n5. **Recurrence:** none. **Attendees:** create-time guests + avatar display only. **Timezone:** user timezone, abbreviation, selectable timezone in composer and display settings.\n6. **Navigation/route:** no `AppPath.Calendar`; calendar is a `ViewType` and a page-layout widget/action; nav items are workspace-defined; related-record action id `create-calendar-event`.\n\nNo files were modified.\n</task_result>\n</task>"
